Implement user story SKY-004-a: Express server routes and middleware implementation

## Story Description
Implement src/server.ts with Express app exporting named `app`, guarded listen(), and four route handlers: GET /health (JSON status), GET / (HTML dashboard from file), GET /search (flight search via SkyscannerClient), GET /cheapest (cheapest flight). Include RAPIDAPI_KEY gate middleware for /search and /cheapest (503 when absent), error handling for SkyscannerClient throws (500), and input validation (400 for missing/invalid params). The searchedAt field in /search responses must be an ISO-8601 datetime reflecting request time. The FlightResult type must be imported from the SKY-002 type export (e.g. src/skyscanner/client.ts), not redeclared inline. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the `listen()` call so supertest can import it without binding a port; the listen() call is guarded by `if (import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href)` (ESM) or `if (require.main === module)` (CJS) matching the tsup output format so vitest never binds a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type application/json and body { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of whether RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is set or absent
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type text/html and response body equal to the contents of src/public/index.html read via fs.readFileSync at runtime — a hardcoded inline HTML string in server.ts that happens to match is NOT acceptable; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search with valid query params (from, to, date, adults) returns HTTP 200 with body { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO-8601 string } where count === flights.length; when adults param is absent it defaults to 1
- GET /search missing any required param (from, to, or date) returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }; non-numeric adults param (e.g. 'abc', '') returns HTTP 400 with body { error: string }
- GET /cheapest with valid required params (from, to, date) returns HTTP 200 with a single FlightResult whose price ≤ all others in the client response; returns HTTP 404 { error: string } when client returns empty array; returns HTTP 400 { error: string } when missing required params; adults defaults to 1 if absent
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent at server initialisation, middleware short-circuits GET /search and GET /cheapest with HTTP 503 Content-Type application/json body { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; GET /health and GET / are unaffected and return normal responses
- When SkyscannerClient throws an error during /search or /cheapest, the server returns HTTP 500 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string } without crashing or emitting an unhandled promise rejection





